* DynaQueueExplorer test setup (on top of the developer defaults: QM1, DEV.APP.SVRCONN, DEV.QUEUE.1..3, DEV.DEAD.LETTER.QUEUE)
ALTER QMGR DEADQ(DEV.DEAD.LETTER.QUEUE) MONQ(MEDIUM)
* TLS only on the application channel, like production. No client certificate required.
ALTER CHANNEL(DEV.APP.SVRCONN) CHLTYPE(SVRCONN) SSLCIPH(ANY_TLS12_OR_HIGHER) SSLCAUTH(OPTIONAL)
* Queues with different message formats, created by tools/perf-env/seed_ibmmq.py
DEFINE QLOCAL(ORDERS.IN) MAXDEPTH(50000) REPLACE
DEFINE QLOCAL(ORDERS.JMS) MAXDEPTH(50000) REPLACE
DEFINE QLOCAL(MAINFRAME.EBCDIC) MAXDEPTH(50000) REPLACE
DEFINE QLOCAL(BINARY.FEED) MAXDEPTH(50000) REPLACE
DEFINE QLOCAL(EMPTY.QUEUE) REPLACE
DEFINE QALIAS(ORDERS.ALIAS) TARGET(ORDERS.IN) REPLACE
DEFINE QREMOTE(PARTNER.ORDERS) RNAME(ORDERS.IN) RQMNAME(QM2) XMITQ(QM2.XMIT) REPLACE
DEFINE QLOCAL(QM2.XMIT) USAGE(XMITQ) REPLACE
* Let the app user (and its group) inquire and browse everything for the explorer, and use the command queue for PCF.
SET AUTHREC PROFILE('**') OBJTYPE(QUEUE) PRINCIPAL('app') AUTHADD(BROWSE,GET,PUT,INQ,DSP,CHG,CLR,PASSALL,SETALL)
* The developer defaults define a more specific DEV.** profile (no display): extend it, or PCF hides the DEV queues.
SET AUTHREC PROFILE('DEV.**') OBJTYPE(QUEUE) PRINCIPAL('app') AUTHADD(BROWSE,GET,PUT,INQ,DSP,CHG,CLR,PASSALL,SETALL)
* A queue the explorer may not see, to exercise partial PCF results.
DEFINE QLOCAL(RESTRICTED.QUEUE) REPLACE
SET AUTHREC PROFILE('RESTRICTED.**') OBJTYPE(QUEUE) PRINCIPAL('app') AUTHADD(NONE)
SET AUTHREC PROFILE('SYSTEM.ADMIN.COMMAND.QUEUE') OBJTYPE(QUEUE) PRINCIPAL('app') AUTHADD(PUT,DSP,INQ)
SET AUTHREC PROFILE('SYSTEM.DEFAULT.MODEL.QUEUE') OBJTYPE(QUEUE) PRINCIPAL('app') AUTHADD(GET,DSP,BROWSE,INQ)
SET AUTHREC OBJTYPE(QMGR) PRINCIPAL('app') AUTHADD(CONNECT,INQ,DSP,SETALL)
REFRESH SECURITY TYPE(CONNAUTH)
